\DOC ENSURES_OR_ENSURES_N_TAC

\TYPE {ENSURES_OR_ENSURES_N_TAC : (goal -> goalstate) -> (goal -> goalstate) -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
A dispatcher that applies one of two supplied tactics to the current goal
according to the form of the goal's conclusion, leaving the assumptions
untouched.

\DESCRIBE
The arguments {tac_for_ensures : goal -> goalstate} and {tac_for_ensures_n :
goal -> goalstate} are two alternative tactics, one of which is selected and
run on the goal. The assumption list {A} is left exactly as it was; only the
conclusion changes, in whatever way the selected tactic changes it. In the
observed traces this yields either one subgoal
{
          A ?- t
   ================= ENSURES_OR_ENSURES_N_TAC tac_for_ensures tac_for_ensures_n
          A ?- u
}
\noindent where {u} is an equivalent reassociated or unfolded form of {t}, or
an existentially quantified or implicational restatement: {u} may begin with
new quantifiers {x1 ... xn} (n possibly zero), or with a new antecedent
discharged from {t}. Alternatively it yields zero subgoals, the goal being
closed outright. No assumptions are added or removed in any observed trace.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces only show goals whose conclusion is a Hoare-triple-style
predicate or an {eventually}-style predicate about machine execution, and in
each case the first of the two argument tactics appears to be the one taking
effect.

\ENDDOC
